From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zero the range bounds before the inputs fill them

RangeFunctionBindData's constructor copies its one to three inputs into
an array of three, and GetParameters() reads at least the first
element. RangeFunctionBind() refuses an empty input list before it
constructs the bind data, so that element is always set, but GCC 10
cannot know that and -Wmaybe-uninitialized reports the read. The array
starts out zeroed, as the engine writes such arrays elsewhere.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/function/table/range.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/function/table/range.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/function/table/range.cpp
index 038189e31b..03d194bdb3 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/function/table/range.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/function/table/range.cpp
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ static void GetParameters(int64_t values[], idx_t value_count, hugeint_t &start,
 
 struct RangeFunctionBindData : public TableFunctionData {
 	explicit RangeFunctionBindData(const vector<Value> &inputs, bool generate_series) : cardinality(0) {
-		int64_t values[3];
+		int64_t values[3] = {};
 		for (idx_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); i++) {
 			if (inputs[i].IsNull()) {
 				return;
